> **عربي:** المشكلة اللي بنحلها

## 1. Problem statement

Today Vigil can show a **mid-execution** todo list (`manage_plan`). That is **not** Cursor Plan Mode.

Users need:

1. Discuss a feature / bug / refactor in chat  
2. Agent (or Plan Mode) produces a **structured plan**  
3. User reviews / edits / reorders / removes steps  
4. User explicitly says **Approve / Execute**  
5. Agent executes **step by step** against that approved plan (visible progress, resumable)

Without this, large work is easy to derail, skip steps, or start coding before alignment.

---

> **عربي:** رحلة المستخدم المثالية

## 2. North-star UX (Vigil Plan Mode)

> **عربي:** أوضاع Plan مقابل Agent

### Modes
- ✅ **Chat / Agent mode** — build & edit (can still call `manage_plan` for ad-hoc loops)
- ✅ **Ask mode** — Cursor-like Ask: discuss / explain codebase; **no writes** (sidecar hard gate)
- ✅ **Plan mode** — planning-first; read/search/investigate; **no writes** until Execute (sidecar hard gate)
- ✅ Clear mode indicator in chat UI (Agent | Ask | Plan)
- ✅ One-click switch between modes (mid-run confirm before switching)
- ✅ **Multi / Multitask** — out of Plan Mode v1 UI; use `delegate_tasks` / parallelizable steps after Execute (see §11)

> **عربي:** قسم — Happy path

### Happy path
1. User: describes goal (Arabic or English)  
2. Vigil enters Plan mode (manual toggle **or** auto-suggest on large/multi-step prompts)  
3. Vigil gathers just enough context (deep index / `parallel_investigate` / open files / rules)  
4. Vigil outputs a **Plan artifact** (not only markdown prose):
   - Title, goal, assumptions, risks
   - Ordered steps with status, optional file hints, optional acceptance checks
5. User can:
   - Edit step text  
   - Add / delete / reorder steps  
   - Mark a step as optional / blocked  
   - Ask to “revise plan” with feedback without executing  
6. User clicks **Execute plan** (or says موافق نفّذ)  
7. Agent runs with the approved plan as **source of truth**:
   - Exactly one `in_progress`  
   - Updates step status as it goes  
   - Does not silently invent a parallel conflicting checklist unless synced into the same plan  
8. On completion: summary mapped to steps (done / skipped / failed) + files changed + tests run

> **عربي:** الحفظ والاستمرارية

### Persistence
- ✅ Plans are **first-class artifacts** (survive tab reload / app restart via `.vigil/plans/`)
- ✅ **Primary storage: Firestore** — owned by Cloud Bridge (`02` / `03`); desktop SoR for v1 remains `.vigil/plans/` until bridge ships
- ✅ Optional local cache / export (`.vigil/plans/` now) — **not** the long-term SoR after Cloud Bridge
- ✅ List past plans; reopen; clone; archive (PlanPanel History)
- ✅ Link plan ↔ chat tab / session id (`chatTabId` on create/sync + UI hint)

> **عربي:** قواعد زر التنفيذ

### Execute semantics
- ✅ Hard gate: **no write_file / apply_patch / push / PR** while in Plan mode before Execute  
- ✅ After Execute: normal tool policies + Auto-run rules still apply (`planExecuteUnlocked` + switch to Agent)  
- ✅ Pause / Resume / Stop mid-plan (`paused` status + PlanPanel controls)  
- ✅ If user interrupts, plan remains with last statuses (chat Stop → pause; turn-end auto-pause)  
- ✅ Failed step: mark `failed`, propose recovery (Retry / Skip & continue / Revise)

---

> **عربي:** شكل بيانات الخطة (الموديل)

## 3. Plan artifact model (target shape)

```text
Plan {
  id, title, goal, status: draft|approved|running|paused|completed|failed|cancelled
  createdAt, updatedAt, workspaceRoot, chatTabId?
  assumptions[], risks[]
  steps: [{
    id, content, status: pending|in_progress|completed|cancelled|failed|skipped
    optional?, parallelizable?, blockedByStepIds[]
    hints: { files[], symbols[], commands[] }
    acceptance?: string
  }]
  execution?: { startedAt, finishedAt, pausedAt, lastError?, failedStepId?, drift? }
  revisions?: [{ at, summary, stepSnapshot[] }]
  archivedAt?
}
```

UI:
- ✅ Plan panel / card richer than today’s `AgentPlanCard` (editable in draft; statuses while running)
- ✅ Diff of plan revisions (v1 → v2 via `revisions` + last-diff preview in PlanPanel)

